### Criterion 1: What does PAEOS need to become genuinely self-hosting?

Self-hosting (FR-9) requires the system to run its own lifecycle on itself. Currently, the planner loop (RE_DERIVE → IDEATE → DESIGN → PLAN) makes engineering decisions without domain research. When PAEOS builds itself, it must research its own architecture, prior art, and constraint space before analyzing trade-offs. **L05 is the first layer that gives the system grounded external/domain knowledge**, rather than relying solely on the model's pre-training.

| Candidate | Self-hosting contribution |
|-----------|--------------------------|
| **A (L05)** | Directly enables informed decision-making; grounds ideation in researched facts rather than model priors. Restores the system's ability to validate ideas against domain reality. |
| **B (L06)** | Enables formal trade-off analysis, but without L05 the trade-offs are based on un-researched assumptions — garbage-in, garbage-out. |
| **C (L09)** | Improves design quality through critique, but is downstream of the core cognition gap (L05-L07). |

